{"title":"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<div style=\"text-align:center\">\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2007_CyMO-23.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/15/2007_CyMO-23.PNG/500px-2007_CyMO-23.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"261\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/15/2007_CyMO-23.PNG/750px-2007_CyMO-23.PNG 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/1/15/2007_CyMO-23.PNG 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p>In the figure above the right section of a parabolic tunnel is presented. Its maximum height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/7/137fce50b87448d28490b60c800d9bd18785e505.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC=8\\,\\mathrm{m}$\" width=\"80\" height=\"12\" /> and its maximum width is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/022f6853cdda6deae5c0a57bf08c6ffef7f89296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=20\\,\\mathrm{m}$\" width=\"89\" height=\"13\" />. If M is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0964c9cf406ef8e5ec8beaa6a92125f2d8f90460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, then the height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/350503b4142c19abeb151a93622b4de560e27171.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MK$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" /> of the tunnel at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e730156d1bccdc58cc2b42a0ad52d7cc441a6fd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ }5\\,\\mathrm{m}\\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 5.2\\,\\mathrm{m}\\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 5.5\\,\\mathrm{m}\\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } 5.8\\,\\mathrm{m}\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 6\\,\\mathrm{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"476\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since it is a parabolic tunnel, the equation of the tunnel is a quadratic. We have three points: (0,8), (10,0), and (-10,0). Since we have both of the roots, we multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/8981dc13c9b6ca534026f2306770641c40a2dbfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(x-10)(x+10)=ax^2-100a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"250\" height=\"19\" />. But we also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/3/123937a5a5c52785a1e2e355f233bc8e67f5619e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-100a=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"84\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/b/04b783c18436124fcd4ccd606cbecbbee53f3137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=.08$\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />. Thus the equation of the parabola is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c621a7a59f3261cd9f89319520821414ab796cea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-.08x^2+8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" />. Now the height of the tunnel at M is the value of the y coordinate when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c80ea5862b45877f08d698a0c893bd2806a2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/3/3a3faf1572d785ef1d5d72f120fb3a16190b4b61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; align:center; width:60%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum\">2007 Cyprus MO, Lyceum</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problems\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_22\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_24\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/